    intro: 'If your dryer gets warm but clothes come out damp — or you\'re running two and three cycles to dry one load — the problem is almost never the heat. It\'s airflow. A dryer dries by pushing hot air THROUGH the clothes and out the vent; when that airflow is choked, the moisture has nowhere to go. This is worth fixing fast, and not just for your laundry: a clogged dryer vent is the #1 cause of dryer fires.',
